.TH COMMAND * 2014-04-08 "SequoiaDB" "Sequoiadb Method's Manual"
.ad l.ll 72.ce 1000
\fBrg.detachNode()\fR
.ce 0
.sp 2

.SH "NAME"

.sp 2
detachNode - Detach a node in the current group.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"

.sp 2

.sp 2

.sp 2
rg.detachNode(\fB<host>\fR,\fB<service>\fR,\fB<options>\fR)
.SH "CATEGORY"

.sp 2

.sp 2
ReplicaGroup
.SH "DESCRIPTION"

.sp 2
Detach a node in the current partition group, but its configuration information will not be deleted. Used with rg.attachNode(). Currently it is possible to support separation of nodes from a data group or a catalog group.

.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp 2
\fBhost (string)\fR
.br
       Specify the host name of the node.
.sp 2
\fBservice (string)\fR
.br
       Node port number.
.sp 2
\fBoptions (json)\fR
.br
       Can be the following options:
.sp 2
       \fB* KeepData (Bool):\fR 
.br
			  Whether to keep the original data of the detached 
              node. This option has no default value. User should 
              specify its value explicitly.
.sp 2
       \fB* enforce (Bool):\fR 
.br
			  Whether to detach the node forcily, default to 
              be false.
.sp 2
\fBNote: \fR
.sp 2
1. The field KeepData in the options must be specified explicitly. For it will determine if the data of the detached node still be kept or not. So, be careful.
.sp 2
2. It can not detach the last node in the replica group unless setting Enforced to be true.
.sp 2
3. The separated nodes will no longer be managed by the cluster. Please join other groups as soon as possible.
			  
.SH "Examples"

.sp 2
1. Detach node from group1 and then add it to group2.
.sp 2
	> var rg1 = db.getRG("group1")
.br
	> rg1.detachNode('hostname1', '11830', {KeepData: true})
.br
	> var rg2 = db.getRG("group2")
.br
	> rg2.attachNode('hostname1', '11830', {KeepData: false})
